{
 "_comment": "Dialogs. Story dialogs are named <level><letter> (0 = the prologue in the forest, 1 cave, 2 forest run, 3 jackpot climb, 4 the PMS maze, M the old meadow, S the old summit) and their lines <level><letter><n>, e.g. 2C3 = level 2, dialog C, line 3; the line's text key in data/i18n/<lang>.json is the same name. A lowercase letter in a level map starts the dialog of that level with that letter (c in level 2 = 2C); A is said when the level starts (except the jackpot climb, where 3A..3D explain the power-ups on the board and 3E ends it there, without buttons). Minigame talk (mg*_start / _after / ...) is not a story dialog and keeps its own names. Edit in Developer mode > Dialogs. Voice file = voice_overrides[key] or <key>.wav in assets/audio.",
